Atlas overlay patch 0070: ui/ui-tokens
Why: the numbers of the window the reel shows: toolbar 36 px (28 px hit area plus 4 px above and below), omnibox 24 px (border included), sidebar rows 28 px with an 8 px inset and radius 6, radii controls 8 / cards 12 / large 16 / window 12 (the radius block of the OS design repo), download glyph 16 px; and one hook line that puts the WolOS tokens on the engine's colours (mixer in chrome/browser/ui/atlas/chrome). The values are the engine's constants and its colour pipeline, so no GN argument, policy or flag reaches them; the logic is in the overlay tree, the patch is hook lines and constants. The hunk in ui/gtk/gtk_color_mixers.cc lets the system theme colour the `toolbar` node (WolOS: `glass`).
Files: chrome/browser/ui/layout_constants.cc, ui/views/layout/layout_provider.cc, chrome/browser/ui/views/helium/frame_corner_radius.cc, chrome/browser/ui/color/chrome_color_mixers.cc, chrome/browser/ui/color/BUILD.gn, ui/gtk/gtk_color_mixers.cc, ui/views/controls/menu/menu_config_linux.cc
Test filter: *AtlasTokens*:*AtlasColorMixer*
Rebase risk: M (layout_constants.cc and layout_provider.cc are also patched by the inherited series, the hunks are single return values; the mixer hook is one line after AddNativeChromeColorMixer)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series touches or adds)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

